  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pulse Lab Jakarta Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Pulse Lab Jakarta (PLJ) was one of the first data innovation labs in the Asia Pacific. The Lab produced prototypes and innovative solutions by harnessing big data, artificial intelligence (AI) and human-centered design for sustainable development and humanitarian action. PLJ was a joint initiative of the United Nations, through United Nations Global Pulse and the Government of Indonesia, through its Ministry of National Development Planning (BAPPENAS). 
PLJ work has directly contributed to Indonesian government key priorities such as: 
(i)	building capacity within the Indonesian Ministry of Health to design data informed countermeasures for the COVID-19 pandemic
(ii)	supporting Indonesia&#x2019;s efforts to create a more inclusive digital economy and addressing inequality of digital access, including for vulnerable groups 
